Note on the brief's own wording for (d): the "Required change" prose says
"When Prev <= 0: `Year N: cut` / `Year N: raise` with NO PERCENTAGE", but acceptance
criterion 2(d) demands "Year 3: cut (90% of plan)". The implementation produces the
criterion-2(d) string. I checked the authoritative surface, the Guardrail Events list
template (web/templates/components/whatif/guardrails.html:100-106): the
`{{if gt .PreviousMultiplier 0.0}}...{{else}}Cut{{end}}` only suppresses the CHANGE
percentage; the `({{printf "%.0f" (mul .Multiplier 100)}}% of plan)` span sits OUTSIDE
that conditional and always renders. So the implementation matches criterion 2(d) AND
matches the existing list surface. Scored on criterion 2(d).

