*** FIXTURE DISCREPANCY IN THE BRIEF (finding, not an implementation defect) ***
The brief states "The live plan's guardrails are 20/10/20/10 with floor 75 / ceiling 120,
and its deterministic projection has a raise at year 15 and cuts at years 29, 33, 35, 37."
That is NOT what the saved plan contains today. From the throwaway copy of the live data:
$ python3 -c "...json.load('/tmp/budget2-whatif-verify-8099/data/settings/whatif.json')..."
    {"enabled": true, "floor_drop_pct": 10, "floor_cut_pct": 10,
     "ceiling_rise_pct": 20, "ceiling_raise_pct": 10,
     "min_spending_pct": 70, "max_spending_pct": 100}
    portfolio 2400000  return 0  years 39  monthly 8900
i.e. 10/10/20/10 with floor 70 / ceiling 100 (max_spending_pct 100 makes a RAISE
impossible by construction), and investment_return 0. The engine therefore produces
exactly ONE guardrail event, not five. This is corroborated by an INDEPENDENT surface on
the same instance — the Guardrail Events list, which this task did not touch:
$ curl http://localhost:8099/whatif   (then tag-stripped)
    ROW: Year 36: Cut by 10% (90% of plan) $28,225.37/mo → $25,402.84/mo
         (today: $7,120.00 → $6,408.00) Portfolio: $3,029,757.20
One row. So the "5 points" in the brief is a stale/incorrect fixture, and the substance of
criterion 5 was verified against the events the engine actually emitted:

  nominal response, "Guardrail cuts / raises":
    x        = [36]
    y        = [3024130.173443734]
    symbol   = ['triangle-down']        (event type "cut" -> correct)
    color    = ['#ef4444']              (cut -> correct)
    size     = 11 ; line = {'color': '#ffffff', 'width': 1}
    type=scatter, mode=markers, hoverinfo='text', cliponaxis=False
    text     = 'Year 36: cut 10% (90% of plan)<br>$28,225.37/mo → $25,402.84/mo'
    "Portfolio Balance" trace y at x==36 = 3024130.173443734   -> MATCH=True (exact, |d|<1e-9)
    layout.yaxis.range = [0, 4059453.1949642524]; max(balance y)=3440214.572003604;
                          3440214.572003604*1.18 = 4059453.1949642524  -> headroom exact.

  real response, same trace:
    x        = [36]
    y        = [762852.8434311618]
    "Portfolio Balance" trace y at x==36 = 762852.8434311618      -> MATCH=True (exact)
    layout.yaxis.range = [0, 2837286.117173364]; max=2404479.76031641; *1.18 = 2837286.117173364
    text     = 'Year 36: cut 10% (90% of plan)<br>$28,225.37/mo → $25,402.84/mo'
               -- IDENTICAL to nominal, i.e. the money is nominal regardless of display
               mode, exactly as the spec requires. (The list's extra "(today: ...)" line is
               correctly NOT in the hover text.)

  Hover money vs. the Guardrail Events list, same instance, same year:
    hover : $28,225.37/mo → $25,402.84/mo
    list  : $28,225.37/mo → $25,402.84/mo      -> byte-identical RENDERED strings.
    Percentages agree too: hover "10% (90% of plan)" vs list "Cut by 10% (90% of plan)".

