────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
OBSERVATIONS (not failures; for the lead's backlog)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
O1. BRIEF FIXTURE STALE (criterion 5). The brief's "guardrails are 20/10/20/10 with floor 75
    / ceiling 120 ... raise at year 15 and cuts at 29, 33, 35, 37" does not describe the
    currently-saved plan (10/10/20/10, floor 70 / ceiling 100, return 0 -> one cut at year 36).
    Any future oracle or checker brief that hardcodes live-plan figures will drift the same way.
O2. The live-server check could not exercise the RAISE marker (triangle-up / #22c55e) because
    max_spending_pct=100 forbids raises in the saved plan. Covered only by unit test 2(b).
O3. The `y <= 0 -> maxBalance * 0.05` fallback (handlers.go:711, mirroring the identical
    Key-events fallback at :673) is implemented per spec but has NO test. It is not one of the
    enumerated acceptance criteria (2a-e), so it is not scored — but it is untested code.
O4. Test 2(c) derives its expectation by calling the same projectionValueAtYear helper the
    implementation calls, which is mildly tautological. Mutations F and H both killed it and
    the failure messages print concrete values (want 1.692e+06 / 1.88e+06) that match the
    fixture's PortfolioBalanceReal/PortfolioBalance by hand, so it is not vacuous in practice.
O5. Criterion 2(a)'s "existing traces unchanged" is verified shallowly (Portfolio Balance
    present + len(y) == len(Months) + stable trace count between nil and empty). It would not
    catch a change to the balance trace's VALUES. Mutation E still killed it.
O6. On the live instance the Guardrail Events list shows "Portfolio: $3,029,757.20" for year 36
    while the chart marker sits at y=3,024,130.17. These are different quantities by design:
    the event's Portfolio field is the balance at the TRIGGER MONTH, the marker y is
    projectionValueAtYear(projection, 36.0) i.e. month 432, which is exactly what the spec
    mandates. Not a defect, but a viewer comparing the two surfaces will see a ~$5.6k gap.
O7. internal/handlers/whatif/handlers.go is listed in .swarm/critical.globs. The task is
    explicitly about that file and is Tier 2 with checks "tests,second" (dual-lane), so the
    touch is authorised; flagged only so the lead sees it acknowledged.
